 {
  "id": "q2-02-exponent-rules-12",
  "lessonId": "q2-02-exponent-rules",
  "type": "PS",
  "difficulty": 5,
  "stem": "For every integer $n$, which of the following is equal to $\\dfrac{5^{n+1}+5^{n}}{5^{n-1}+5^{n-2}}$?",
  "content": {
   "format": "select_one",
   "choices": [
    {
     "id": "A",
     "text": "$5$"
    },
    {
     "id": "B",
     "text": "$6$"
    },
    {
     "id": "C",
     "text": "$25$"
    },
    {
     "id": "D",
     "text": "$125$"
    },
    {
     "id": "E",
     "text": "$625$"
    }
   ]
  },
  "answer": {
   "choices": [
    "C"
   ]
  },
  "explanation": "Factor the lowest power out of each sum: numerator $5^n(5+1)=6\\cdot5^n$; denominator $5^{n-2}(5+1)=6\\cdot5^{n-2}$. The 6s cancel and $5^n/5^{n-2}=5^2=25$.",
  "choiceExplanations": {
   "A": "This compares adjacent exponents ($n+1$ versus $n$) instead of top versus bottom.",
   "B": "6 is the factor that cancels; it is not what remains.",
   "D": "This pairs $5^{n+1}$ with $5^{n-2}$ only.",
   "E": "This treats the sums as products: $5^{2n+1}/5^{2n-3}$."
  },
  "estSeconds": 150,
  "skills": [
   "exponent-rules"
  ],
  "review": {
